From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: Add a /run tier to the texi2any and texinfo config directory search
Source: Nex package maintainers
Upstream: not submitted; this codifies a Nex-specific UAPI layering rule

texi2any.pl builds its texi2any-config.pm and texinfo language config
search lists from the user directories, $sysconfdir/texinfo(or
texi2any), and $datadir/texinfo(or texi2any), loaded from lowest to
highest priority (curdir and $HOME beat $sysconfdir, which beats
$datadir). Nex layers configuration across /usr (vendor defaults),
/run (runtime overlay), and /etc (administrator overrides), with /etc
winning over /run winning over /usr. Insert a /run/texinfo and
/run/texi2any tier between $sysconfdir and $datadir so /etc keeps
priority over /run, and /run keeps priority over the vendor tree in
$datadir.

--- a/tp/texi2any.pl
+++ b/tp/texi2any.pl
@@ -378,6 +378,7 @@
                                 if (defined($ENV{'HOME'}));
 push @language_config_dirs, File::Spec->catdir($sysconfdir, 'texinfo')
                                if (defined($sysconfdir));
+push @language_config_dirs, File::Spec->catdir('/run', 'texinfo');
 push @language_config_dirs, File::Spec->catdir($datadir, 'texinfo')
                                if (defined($datadir));
 my @texinfo_config_dirs = ($curdir, @language_config_dirs);
@@ -392,6 +393,7 @@
        if (defined($ENV{'HOME'}));
 push @program_config_dirs, File::Spec->catdir($sysconfdir, $program_name)
        if (defined($sysconfdir));
+push @program_config_dirs, File::Spec->catdir('/run', $program_name);
 push @program_config_dirs, File::Spec->catdir($datadir, $program_name)
   if (defined($datadir));

